<section id="markets">
<h2>🏦 International Financial Markets</h2>
<p class="sub">Where MNCs trade currencies and raise money, and where FX risk is created and managed</p>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card" style="background:linear-gradient(160deg,var(--card),rgba(24,195,176,.22))"><div class="big">💱</div><h3>Foreign Exchange Market</h3><p>Where currencies are bought and sold: spot, forwards, swaps, and options. Banks, companies, and central banks all take part.</p><div class="link">🏢 MNC link: converting sales, paying suppliers, hedging.</div></div>
<div class="card" style="background:linear-gradient(160deg,var(--card),rgba(108,76,255,.2))"><div class="big">🏧</div><h3>Eurocurrency Market</h3><p>Banks take deposits and make loans in a currency outside its home country (e.g. USD deposits held in London). "Euro" here does not mean only Europe.</p><div class="link">🏢 MNC link: short and medium-term funding.</div></div>
<div class="card" style="background:linear-gradient(160deg,var(--card),rgba(255,77,141,.2))"><div class="big">📜</div><h3>International Bond Market</h3><p><b>Foreign bonds</b> are issued by a foreign borrower in the local market and currency. <b>Eurobonds</b> are issued outside the country of the currency they are denominated in.</p><div class="link">🏢 MNC link: long-term debt, choice of currency.</div></div>
<div class="card" style="background:linear-gradient(160deg,var(--card),rgba(255,201,51,.3))"><div class="big">📈</div><h3>International Stock Market</h3><p>Firms raise equity abroad by cross-listing shares on foreign exchanges or through depositary receipts such as ADRs.</p><div class="link">🏢 MNC link: investors, visibility, equity funding.</div></div>
</div>
<div class="note" style="max-width:100%">Think: when your MNC borrows or raises equity in a foreign currency, does it <i>reduce</i> or <i>create</i> FX exposure? Keep this in mind for Questions 1 to 3.</div>
</section>

